  meeting with with questions or this is  what you're thinking correct or reminder  you know that kind of thing and it's  just it's ongoing all the way up to a  game time your team had reached the  level of domination in recent weeks that  reminded me of when we were growing up  in the 70s and scores would be fifty  three to ten and forty eight to three  and and and it was going incredibly well  and then last Thursday night a pothole  emerged with the Dallas Cowboys now that  you've had a week to look back on that  game what's your assessment of what  happened that night in Dallas well I  would say this if it really unfolded  from a scoring standpoint we felt I felt  it was going to be a lower scoring game  their defense is playing good football  and I kicked myself for two or three  different situations in that game of not  really not handling them the right way  and you know we have an opportunity to  score its fourth and two and I know our  fourth down numbers are good and I felt  like we had a good plan and yet in that  type of game kicked a field goal because  III didn't feel that was going to be a  30-something two twenty-something game  at all I felt going in patients was  going to have to be you know something  that we valued ball security and we were  able to you know get the takeaways  defensively field position in the  kicking game so that we can say the  first thing I'd say is I don't want to  shortchange what I think is a much  improved Cowboys team that played won  three in a row and just won or fourth  and and they're playing exceptionally  well and then from our standpoint me of  managing that a little bit better and  you know you come away with a tough road  win and regardless of how it happened it  happened in Baltimore 21 20 you know  that type of game I just felt like it  was going to be a lower scoring game and  yet I didn't manage it the same way you  touched on a very compelling top it can  vary Tommy now in the NFL I spoke to  Doug  the Eagles coach recently about this all  the factors that come into play when  you're making that decision on fourth  down go for it or not going for to go  for it or not give us an idea of  everything that's in your own personal  stew of what influences your decision in  those moments are already option whether  or not you think it's obvious question  what all goes into great question  because this is the challenge and this  is what looking in this is what will  drive the analysts crazy and yet the  numbers and the situations relative to  the percentages are important but how do  we feel like with our play inventory at  that point in the game so if I'm inside  the 5-yard line and I've got a section  of two-point plays that let's say I love  two of these I mean I love them well  certainly I would love them enough to  score six points with them right I mean  I'm not going to as much as I love this  play from the two I'm going to wait in  case we need it in the second half for  four so I'm like hey I don't know how  many times I'm going to be inside that  five and if I if this is a two-point  play but it also is a play I like you  know we'll call it in the first quarter  to score touchdown so what's your play  inventory like at that point relative to  where you're at in the game and this  that would be more inside the five and  two point play or going for it  how's the game going you know I honestly  and I'm old-school this way I'm not  interested in that two-point chart in a  lower scoring game in the third quarter  I'm not and and so now in a higher  scoring game I'm gonna look at that  chart a little earlier and yet it still  wouldn't be well into the second half  now fourth down 38 yard line who will be  playing how are we matching up you know  I was asked the question once about a  game four years ago and why why didn't  you consider and I said well  have you looked at the matchup over at  our left tackle position and so during  the course of that game that matchup was  