 and it's it's part of  this program to make the punts safer  they're crowdsourcing ideas there's a  lot of confusion about what's wrong with  the punt as it's currently configured do  you have a feel for why there's an  urgency to change the punt play to make  the punt play more safer and what's  dangerous about the punt in comparison  you know kickoff I I don't know  specifically I would say the one unusual  thing about the punt play and this I  think we'll see change in the next five  years it's the only play where these  Gunners potentially will literally fly  through the sidelines back up and they  get forced out of bounds and then the  jammers have to run not in the white but  wait for them to come back in the field  of play to hit them so it's the only  play where there's elements to the punt  coverage unit that are played on the  sidelines not in the field and and  you've seen you've seen crazy looks for  that that jammer goes behind three  players in the bench and pops out you  know later on down the sidelines so I  think I don't have the numbers though  statistically relative to injuries and  and I listed I saw the you know come up  with an idea and submit it and that  whole thing and and it's all good well  we'll see what they do with that coach  and we'll see how the rest of the season  goes for you wish you all the best I  know you're really busy I'll let you get  back to work  and we look forward to talking to you  again soon it sounds good  all right Mike thanks  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

